# Keep the build context small and free of local state. Both Dockerfiles use the repo
# root as context (see docker-compose.yml), so without this file the multi-GB .venv,
# node_modules, the dev .next build and the local SQLite database would all be sent to
# the daemon, and `COPY web/ ./` would carry web/.env.local into the image.
.git
.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
*.egg-info
web/.next
web/out
*.tsbuildinfo
data
docs
.worktrees
.playwright-cli
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
